# Testing and CI

How the library is checked: host tests, compiled documentation, an install test, the examples and static analysis,
on every pull request.

## Host tests

```bash
cmake -S . -B build -DXMPL100_BUILD_TESTS=ON
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

| File | Covers |
| --- | --- |
| [`tests/host/test_moving_average.cpp`](../tests/host/test_moving_average.cpp) | Lifecycle, window, rejection, errors |
| [`tests/host/test_errors.cpp`](../tests/host/test_errors.cpp) | Every `Error` value is returned by some call |
| [`tests/host/test_version.cpp`](../tests/host/test_version.cpp) | The version getters follow the generated header |
| [`tests/host/test_kconfig.cpp`](../tests/host/test_kconfig.cpp) | `KconfigDefaults()` with and without `CONFIG_` values |
| [`tests/check_install.cmake`](../tests/check_install.cmake) | Installs and builds [`tests/install_consumer/`](../tests/install_consumer/CMakeLists.txt) with `find_package(xmpl100)` |

The tests build with `-fno-exceptions -fno-rtti` and warnings as errors, on GCC and Clang. Every C++ block on this
site is included from [`tests/docs/`](../tests/docs/quickstart.cpp), which the same build compiles.

## CI workflows

[`ci.yml`](../.github/workflows/ci.yml) runs the host tests and the host example, the MCU example builds, the docs
build, clang-format and clang-tidy, cppcheck, Markdown and YAML lint, then the `CI gate` job: the one required check,
`CI gate / gate`.